A part line is one part: the path its matcher reads, as direct child
steps from the page for a root part and from the part above it for any
other, and how many subtrees it matched in the page. A field line is
one field: the path its matcher reads inside the subtree, self when it
reads that subtree itself, and in how many subtrees it found a node.
Under it are up to 3 of the values it read. A blob line points at the
appendix at the end of the file instead, because what a blob holds is
the text of a whole run of nodes rather than a level of the page.
A path longer than 160 characters is cut.

